# pipanel device configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # then edit .env for THIS device
#
# .env is gitignored, so each Pi keeps its own settings and update.sh's
# `git reset --hard` can't wipe them. deploy.sh writes PIPANEL_SCREEN for you:
#
#   sudo ./deploy.sh --screen waveshare144
#
# A real environment variable overrides the file for one run:
#
#   PIPANEL_SCREEN=1080TV python3 main.py

# --- Screen ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Which profile from profiles.json to drive. Applies to main.py, to the apps
# run standalone (python3 apps/pong.py), and to deploy.sh's per-screen setup.
#
#   waveshare144  Waveshare 1.44" LCD HAT — 128x128 ST7735S over SPI + GPIO
#   35panel       3.5" SPI TFT on /dev/fb1 — 480x320 framebuffer
#   1080TV        HDMI output on /dev/fb0 — 1920x1080 framebuffer
#
# List what the checked-out profiles.json offers with: ./deploy.sh --list
PIPANEL_SCREEN=waveshare144

# --- Apps ------------------------------------------------------------------
# WeatherAPI key for the WEATHER app (https://www.weatherapi.com/). Leave empty
# to run the panel without weather.
WEATHER_API_KEY=
